body:
All CI jobs (lint, build, test, docs) were failing due to two issues in `packages/fields/src/widgets/FileField.tsx`:

- **`react-hooks/rules-of-hooks`**: Four `useCallback` hooks were called after an `if (readonly) return` early return, violating Rules of Hooks
- **TS7006**: Implicit `any` on parameter `t` in `.map()` / `.some()` callbacks under `strict: true`

The fields package build failure cascaded to all downstream packages since turbo resolves `^build` dependencies.

### Fix

Moved all hooks and the `files` variable above the `readonly` early return. Added explicit `string` type annotations.

```tsx
// Before (broken): hooks after early return
const [isDragOver, setIsDragOver] = useState(false);

if (readonly) { return <span>...</span>; }  // ← early return

const processFiles = useCallback(...);       // ← rules-of-hooks violation
const handleDrop = useCallback((e) => {
  accept.split(',').map(t => t.trim());      // ← implicit any
}, ...);

// After (fixed): hooks before early return
const [isDragOver, setIsDragOver] = useState(false);
const files = value ? (Array.isArray(value) ? value : [value]) : [];
const processFiles = useCallback(...);
const handleDrop = useCallback((e) => {
  accept.split(',').map((t: string) => t.trim());
}, ...);

if (readonly) { return <span>...</span>; }
```

